-- Illustrations
-- =============================================================================

§ `Illustrations`

§§ `39 -- illustrations`

`a proven attack before the offence court` MEANS `S39 Application Facts` WITH
    `attack by a dog is shown on the balance of probabilities to have caused injury or damage` IS TRUE
    , `the matter is before a court hearing an offence arising out of that attack` IS TRUE
    , `application is to the Magistrates Court, made by a local government` IS FALSE
    , `application is to the Magistrates Court, made by an authorised person` IS FALSE
    , `application is to the Magistrates Court, made by a person specifically authorised by a local government for the purposes of s 33E` IS FALSE

`a proven attack, local government applies to the Magistrates Court` MEANS `S39 Application Facts` WITH
    `attack by a dog is shown on the balance of probabilities to have caused injury or damage` IS TRUE
    , `the matter is before a court hearing an offence arising out of that attack` IS FALSE
    , `application is to the Magistrates Court, made by a local government` IS TRUE
    , `application is to the Magistrates Court, made by an authorised person` IS FALSE
    , `application is to the Magistrates Court, made by a person specifically authorised by a local government for the purposes of s 33E` IS FALSE

`an unproven attack` MEANS `S39 Application Facts` WITH
    `attack by a dog is shown on the balance of probabilities to have caused injury or damage` IS FALSE
    , `the matter is before a court hearing an offence arising out of that attack` IS TRUE
    , `application is to the Magistrates Court, made by a local government` IS FALSE
    , `application is to the Magistrates Court, made by an authorised person` IS FALSE
    , `application is to the Magistrates Court, made by a person specifically authorised by a local government for the purposes of s 33E` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `a court or the Magistrates Court may order destruction under s 39(1)` `a proven attack before the offence court`
#ASSERT `a court or the Magistrates Court may order destruction under s 39(1)` `a proven attack, local government applies to the Magistrates Court`
#ASSERT NOT (`a court or the Magistrates Court may order destruction under s 39(1)` `an unproven attack`)

#ASSERT `the person may give effect to the s 39 order for destruction` `order that the dog be destroyed by a person specifically authorised by the court` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the person may give effect to the s 39 order for destruction` `order that the dog be destroyed by a person specifically authorised by the court` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the person may give effect to the s 39 order for destruction` `order that the owner destroy the dog or cause it to be destroyed` TRUE)

`a court order with an unmet action requirement` MEANS `S39 Requirement Facts` WITH
    `court has made an order that the dog is to be destroyed` IS TRUE
    , `owner required to take specified action, within the period specified in the order, to prevent or reduce the likelihood of the dog causing injury, or to enable effect to be given to the order for destruction` IS TRUE
    , `owner complied with that action requirement within the period specified in the order` IS FALSE
    , `owner required to pay costs or expenses incurred in relation to the detention or destruction of the dog` IS FALSE
    , `owner paid those costs or expenses` IS FALSE

`a court order fully complied with` MEANS `S39 Requirement Facts` WITH
    `court has made an order that the dog is to be destroyed` IS TRUE
    , `owner required to take specified action, within the period specified in the order, to prevent or reduce the likelihood of the dog causing injury, or to enable effect to be given to the order for destruction` IS TRUE
    , `owner complied with that action requirement within the period specified in the order` IS TRUE
    , `owner required to pay costs or expenses incurred in relation to the detention or destruction of the dog` IS TRUE
    , `owner paid those costs or expenses` IS TRUE

`a court order with an unmet costs requirement only` MEANS `S39 Requirement Facts` WITH
    `court has made an order that the dog is to be destroyed` IS TRUE
    , `owner required to take specified action, within the period specified in the order, to prevent or reduce the likelihood of the dog causing injury, or to enable effect to be given to the order for destruction` IS TRUE
    , `owner complied with that action requirement within the period specified in the order` IS TRUE
    , `owner required to pay costs or expenses incurred in relation to the detention or destruction of the dog` IS TRUE
    , `owner paid those costs or expenses` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `s 39(3) offence -- owner fails to comply with the court's requirement` `a court order with an unmet action requirement`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 39(3) offence -- owner fails to comply with the court's requirement` `a court order fully complied with`)
-- exercises the (b) costs-requirement disjunct on its own, with the (a)
-- action requirement fully satisfied.
#ASSERT `s 39(3) offence -- owner fails to comply with the court's requirement` `a court order with an unmet costs requirement only`
#ASSERT `s 39(3) penalty` EQUALS Penalty WITH fine IS JUST 5_000, `minimum fine` IS NOTHING, `imprisonment months` IS NOTHING, `further offence fine` IS NOTHING

`a two-dog attack, this dog took part` MEANS `Multi-Dog Attack Facts` WITH
    `attack by 2 or more dogs is shown on the balance of probabilities to have caused injury or damage` IS TRUE
    , `this dog took part in the attack` IS TRUE
    , `possible to show which of the dogs actually caused the injury or damage` IS FALSE

`a two-dog attack, this dog was not involved` MEANS `Multi-Dog Attack Facts` WITH
    `attack by 2 or more dogs is shown on the balance of probabilities to have caused injury or damage` IS TRUE
    , `this dog took part in the attack` IS FALSE
    , `possible to show which of the dogs actually caused the injury or damage` IS TRUE

-- s 39(4) witness: even though it is NOT possible to show which dog actually
-- caused the injury (the third field is FALSE/TRUE respectively, and read
-- by neither assertion), attribution turns only on the group-attack finding
-- and this dog's participation in it.
#ASSERT `the dog is treated, for the purposes of s 39(1), as having caused the injury or damage` `a two-dog attack, this dog took part`
#ASSERT NOT (`the dog is treated, for the purposes of s 39(1), as having caused the injury or damage` `a two-dog attack, this dog was not involved`)

§§ `40 -- illustrations`

`an application for destruction is before the court` MEANS `S40 Jurisdiction Facts` WITH
    `application made for an order for the destruction of the dog` IS TRUE
    , `in the proceedings before the court or the State Administrative Tribunal, the destruction of the dog may be ordered` IS FALSE

`neither an application nor a proceeding where destruction may be ordered` MEANS `S40 Jurisdiction Facts` WITH
    `application made for an order for the destruction of the dog` IS FALSE
    , `in the proceedings before the court or the State Administrative Tribunal, the destruction of the dog may be ordered` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the court or the State Administrative Tribunal has jurisdiction to make orders under s 40(1)` `an application for destruction is before the court`
#ASSERT NOT (`the court or the State Administrative Tribunal has jurisdiction to make orders under s 40(1)` `neither an application nor a proceeding where destruction may be ordered`)

-- every s 40(1) limb (bar (ea)) is available on the same jurisdiction fact,
-- regardless of which limb is asked about -- s 40(1)(c)'s "whether or not an
-- order is made for the destruction of the dog" witness.
#ASSERT `the court or the State Administrative Tribunal may include this limb in a s 40(1) order` `an application for destruction is before the court` `order the seizure and detention of the dog`
#ASSERT `the court or the State Administrative Tribunal may include this limb in a s 40(1) order` `an application for destruction is before the court` `order the destruction of the dog`
#ASSERT NOT (`the court or the State Administrative Tribunal may include this limb in a s 40(1) order` `neither an application nor a proceeding where destruction may be ordered` `give all necessary directions to make the order effective`)

#ASSERT `the court or the State Administrative Tribunal may make a cost order under s 40(1)(ea)` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `the court or the State Administrative Tribunal may make a cost order under s 40(1)(ea)` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the court or the State Administrative Tribunal may make a cost order under s 40(1)(ea)` FALSE FALSE)

`a fully compliant destruction order` MEANS `S40 Destruction Order Statement` WITH
    `states to whom the order is directed` IS TRUE
    , `states whether or not the order may be remitted, and if so in what circumstances` IS TRUE
    , `states the period within which it is to be put into effect` IS TRUE

`a destruction order silent on the period` MEANS `S40 Destruction Order Statement` WITH
    `states to whom the order is directed` IS TRUE
    , `states whether or not the order may be remitted, and if so in what circumstances` IS TRUE
    , `states the period within which it is to be put into effect` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the s 40 destruction order satisfies its content requirements` `a fully compliant destruction order`
#ASSERT NOT (`the s 40 destruction order satisfies its content requirements` `a destruction order silent on the period`)

`a humane, speedy destruction` MEANS `S40 Execution Facts` WITH
    `destruction was effected so far as is practicable without cruelty` IS TRUE
    , `destruction was effected by some speedy means` IS TRUE

`a cruel destruction` MEANS `S40 Execution Facts` WITH
    `destruction was effected so far as is practicable without cruelty` IS FALSE
    , `destruction was effected by some speedy means` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `the destruction was effected in accordance with s 40(3)` `a humane, speedy destruction`
#ASSERT NOT (`the destruction was effected in accordance with s 40(3)` `a cruel destruction`)

`ownership changed, no variation application` MEANS `S40 Variation Facts` WITH
    `ownership of the dog has changed, or is not known` IS TRUE
    , `dog is no longer kept in the area for which the local government is the registration authority` IS FALSE
    , `application made to the court or tribunal that made the original order` IS FALSE
    , `court or tribunal is satisfied the changed circumstances are such that the order may be varied` IS FALSE

`ownership changed, variation application succeeds` MEANS `S40 Variation Facts` WITH
    `ownership of the dog has changed, or is not known` IS TRUE
    , `dog is no longer kept in the area for which the local government is the registration authority` IS FALSE
    , `application made to the court or tribunal that made the original order` IS TRUE
    , `court or tribunal is satisfied the changed circumstances are such that the order may be varied` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `the s 40 order must be implemented notwithstanding the change in circumstances` `ownership changed, no variation application`
#ASSERT NOT (`the s 40 order must be implemented notwithstanding the change in circumstances` `ownership changed, variation application succeeds`)

#ASSERT `the person complied with the s 40(5) duty to dispose of the carcass` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the person complied with the s 40(5) duty to dispose of the carcass` FALSE)

§§ `41 -- illustrations`

`lawful destruction measures` MEANS `S41 Indemnity Facts` WITH
    `measures were lawfully taken for the destruction of a dog under this Act` IS TRUE

`unlawful destruction measures` MEANS `S41 Indemnity Facts` WITH
    `measures were lawfully taken for the destruction of a dog under this Act` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the person is indemnified under s 41 against action, claim, demand or an offence, by reason only of the destruction measures` `lawful destruction measures`
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is indemnified under s 41 against action, claim, demand or an offence, by reason only of the destruction measures` `unlawful destruction measures`)
